@title Settlement Consumer Lag Runbook
@subtitle settlement-consumer group on payments-events
@author Streaming team, Corvid Payments

## Alert thresholds

table = Severity,Lag (messages),Duration,Action; Warning,"50,000",10 minutes,Slack only; Critical,"250,000",5 minutes,page on-call; Emergency,"1,000,000",any,page on-call and the Streaming lead

## Triage flow

diagram triage dir=TB title="Consumer lag triage"
triage: alert "Lag alert fires" user
triage: running "Consumers running?" svc focus
triage: restart "Restart consumers" fn
triage: skew "Partition skew?" svc focus
triage: rebalance "Rebalance partitions" fn
triage: scale "Scale out consumers" fn
triage: recover "Lag recovering" svc
triage: alert -> running
triage: running -> restart : no
triage: running -> skew : yes
triage: skew -> rebalance : yes
triage: skew -> scale : no
triage: restart -> recover
triage: rebalance -> recover
triage: scale -> recover

## Steps

1. Check the consumer pods in the `streaming` namespace.
2. Check per-partition lag.
3. If one partition holds more than 40% of the lag, treat it as skew.
4. Scale the deployment to at most 24 replicas, because the topic has 24 partitions.

!!! **Never reset consumer offsets to latest.** Unprocessed settlements would be skipped and would have to be reconciled by hand.

! **Escalation:** if lag is still growing after 30 minutes, escalate to the Streaming lead.
